    "twelve.steps.title": "The Twelve Steps",
    "twelve.steps.lede": "The path AHA walks — read slowly, one Step at a time. They are suggestions born of experience, not commandments.",
    "twelve.steps.foot": "Adapted for AHA from the Twelve Steps of Alcoholics Anonymous, which A.A. neither endorses nor is affiliated with this adaptation.",
    "twelve.traditions.title": "The Twelve Traditions",
    "twelve.traditions.lede": "How Circles stay whole. The Steps carry the member; the Traditions carry the fellowship.",
    "twelve.traditions.foot": "Adapted for AHA from the Twelve Traditions of Alcoholics Anonymous, which A.A. neither endorses nor is affiliated with this adaptation.",
    "twelve.step.1": "We admitted we had been disconnected from our roots and ourselves, and that our lives had become unmanageable.",
    "twelve.step.2": "We came to believe that there are spiritual powers greater than ourselves that could restore us to unity.",
    "twelve.step.3": "We made a decision to turn our life and will to our higher powers, as we understood them.",
    "twelve.step.4": "We made peace with the swing of things — the departure and the return, the loss and the recovery — and learned to breathe steady while the tide moves us.",
    "twelve.step.5": "We accepted that the world we experience is shaped by the mind, and that to change our life we had to learn journeying through it.",
    "twelve.step.6": "We learned to read the world around us and the world within us by journeying into our lower world as well as into the upper world. We found there a reflection of what is here.",
    "twelve.step.7": "We finally faced the opposites we had sometimes refused — fear and courage, femininity and masculinity, ancestor and self — and learned that they are one thing scaling in degrees.",
    "twelve.step.8": "We took honest and fearless inventory of our lives, owned our part without excuse, admitted to our spirits and to another human being the nature of our dis-ease, then made amends when compassionately possible.",
    "twelve.step.9": "We accepted that we are not fixed things but moving energy, and began the daily practice of raising and sustaining our state — through breath, drum, stillness, and ritual — turning, a little more each day, toward who we were becoming.",
    "twelve.step.10": "We experience the last breath of the past and welcome the first of the new. The sacred time is a circle, our horizon is a circle, we are a circle. We are reborn.",
    "twelve.step.11": "We honestly assessed ourselves daily and when we were wrong promptly admitted it. We try to deepen our contact with our higher spiritual powers, praying only for knowledge of their will for us and the power to carry that out.",
    "twelve.step.12": "Having had a spiritual awakening as the result of these Steps, we carry the message to other human beings and we practice these principles in every part of our lives.",
    "twelve.tradition.1": "Our common welfare should come first. Awakening and personal recovery depend upon AHA unity. It is the circle that keeps the flame alive in each of us.",
    "twelve.tradition.2": "For our circle purpose there is but one ultimate authority, a set of compassionate spirits as they may express themselves during our group conscience. AHA has no leaders, but trusted servants; they assist but do not govern.",
    "twelve.tradition.3": "The only requirement for AHA membership is a desire to spiritually progress by asking yourself “Who do you think you are?”",
    "twelve.tradition.4": "Each circle should be autonomous except in matters affecting other circles or AHA as a whole.",
    "twelve.tradition.5": "Each group has but one primary purpose: to carry its message to any human being who still suffers.",
    "twelve.tradition.6": "An AHA circle ought never endorse, finance, or lend the AHA name to any related facility or outside enterprise, lest problems of money, property, and prestige divert us from our primary purpose.",
    "twelve.tradition.7": "Every Circle ought to be fully self-supporting, declining outside contributions.",
    "twelve.tradition.8": "AHA should remain forever nonprofessional, but our service centers may employ special workers.",
    "twelve.tradition.9": "AHA circles, as such, ought never be organized; but we may create service boards or committees directly responsible to those they serve.",
    "twelve.tradition.10": "AHA has no opinion on outside issues; hence the AHA name ought never be drawn into public controversy.",
    "twelve.tradition.11": "Our public relations policy is based on attraction rather than promotion; we need always maintain personal anonymity at the level of new media, press, radio, and films.",
    "twelve.tradition.12": "Anonymity is the spiritual foundation of all our traditions, ever reminding us to place principles before personalities.",
    "create.gate.sponsorTitle": "It is too early to create a Circle",
    "create.gate.sponsorBody": "Your sponsor has not validated you yet. A Circle is founded by a validated member, so this step waits for that validation. Once your sponsor's validation is done, you can create your Circle here.",
    "create.gate.sponsorAction": "Go to My Circle",
